*_nottrack*
doc_1/
docs/
.tmp/
*_old
*.log*
*.log
old/
*_corrupted*
__pycache__/
*.q
# ...but NOT the benchmark queries. They are the benchmark definition -- hand-curated per family,
# with the reasoning in benchmarks/queries/*/README -- not a runtime artefact. The bare `*.q`
# above predates them being added, so the 22 committed before it survived while every query
# written since was silently untracked: benchmarks/queries/reach/hddi.q (the `A[] true` fix) and
# benchmarks/queries/live/hddi.q both existed only on one machine.
!benchmarks/queries/**/*.q
*pid
STOP
*pgid
# Benchmark runtime artefacts: driver logs and the pid/pgid/STOP markers of a live sweep.
# A committed STOP silently kills the next run, so these must never be tracked.
benchmarks/**/*.log
benchmarks/**/bench.pid
benchmarks/**/bench.pgid
benchmarks/**/STOP

*backup*
*_old.csv

shard*
*shard*
hddi/
# hora E[] sharded sweep (benchmarks/scripts/hora_eg_shards.py): only the MERGED table
# benchmarks/results/eg/hora/hora_eg_t1.csv is tracked. Each per-family shard directory holds
# its own partial CSV, seed and driver log -- working files of one run, superseded the moment
# `hora_eg_shards.py merge` folds them in, and meaningless on any other machine.
benchmarks/results/eg/hora/*/
benchmarks/scripts/hora_exact.sh
benchmarks/results/eg/hora/twolock_seed.csv
benchmarks/results/reach.zip
benchmarks/results/eg/hora/forward.csv
benchmarks/results/eg/hora_gfp_back/backward.csv
benchmarks/results/live/hora/forward.csv
benchmarks/results/live/hora_backward/backward.csv
